From: qcom-toolbox <169756160+qcom-toolbox@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] init: reboot to recovery even without a misc partition

On devices without a misc partition writing the BCB fails, and init
returned without rebooting at all. Samsung bootloaders select recovery
from the kernel reboot reason, so log the failure and carry on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YHmiQGxHgHmd9D8TNUemvH
---
diff --git a/init/reboot.cpp b/init/reboot.cpp
index a1eecbf..d686cdb 100644
--- a/init/reboot.cpp
+++ b/init/reboot.cpp
@@ -1124,8 +1124,9 @@ void HandlePowerctlMessage(const std::string& command) {
                 if (!CommandIsPresent(&boot)) {
                     strlcpy(boot.command, "boot-recovery", sizeof(boot.command));
                     if (std::string err; !write_bootloader_message(boot, &err)) {
+                        // Devices without a misc partition (e.g. Samsung, whose
+                        // bootloader takes the kernel reboot reason) still reboot.
                         LOG(ERROR) << "Failed to set bootloader message: " << err;
-                        return;
                     }
                 }
             } else if (std::find(cmd_params.begin(), cmd_params.end(), "quiescent") !=
